## Star topology (Bible §13.1, §4.10)

- **Pope client** — single writer and source of truth. Ranks, records, ceremony state, Chronicle: modified only in the Pope's store.
- **Congregation clients** — display terminals plus input devices. They render broadcast state and send inputs (petitions, favor, confession text) to the Pope's console. Inputs never trigger public theater.
- **Witnesses report, never rule.** No distributed consensus, no peer self-reported authority. One writer: no conflicts in MVP.

State broadcasts one-way on the guild addon channel with sequence numbers. Theatrical UI renders only from a registered Pope-character sender; congregation-originated messages are console inputs only; player-typed free text renders only on the Pope's console. Messages carry a protocol version; stale clients degrade to Quiet Mode rather than misrender theater (§13.4).

## Ceremony runtime (Bible §20)

States, named only: **QUIET → ASSEMBLY → RITE (typed) → CONSEQUENCE → ASSEMBLY or QUIET**. The Pope's client owns every transition. Event Mode theater (Gora, fight HUD, Knighting) hangs on this skeleton. The Director Console starts events from QUIET (§20.2). The Nights board is Quiet Mode, player-opened (§14.1). Records Book is player-opened identity/history (§14.2). Detail: `ceremony-runtime.mdc`.

